{#
  CLOSE: the hero, answered, and the way in. The page opened with
  ALVSolutions' words in the key light; it ends the same way, with the
  words in the light and, beside them, the live site's project intake form
  (components/quote-form.njk, the same partial /contact/ renders, so every
  question and step is identical). The three "what happens next" items sit
  under the words (components/contact-next.njk).

  .h-quote scopes the form's Screen Light styling (home.css); its
  behaviour is src/forms/quote-wizard.ts, bundled into home.js. The package
  and build pickers above still submit to /contact/?package=, where the
  same form picks the choice up.

  The key rises as the ending arrives (src/home/close.ts); at rest, and with
  motion off, it is simply up.
#}
<section class="room h-close" id="start" aria-labelledby="start-h" data-room="close">
  <div class="room-light" aria-hidden="true"><span class="key-cone"></span><span class="key-pool"></span></div>
  <div class="h-close-in h-quote h-wrap">
    <div class="h-close-copy">
      <h2 id="start-h" class="lit-display h-close-h" data-lit>Tell me what the business does.</h2>
      <p>Free quote, no pressure. Three short steps, then a summary you can check before anything sends. I review the project and send you a clear quote and next steps.</p>
      {% include "components/contact-next.njk" %}
    </div>
    <div class="h-close-form" id="quote">
      {% include "components/quote-form.njk" %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
